<h1>Expertise</h1>


<p>As of late I have not been going to a gym to train.
	I have had a good time training with Karate and Kickboxing but in recent days I tried Muay Thai.
</p>

<p>As someone who focuses mainly on my movement, I didn't do well in a normal Muay Thai sparring setting where the goal is stand in front of the other person and throw. 
	THATS NOT ME!</p>

<p>I HATE Muay Thai because it makes you plotty.</p>
	

<p>You will often see Muay Thai fighters throw something like punch, punch, elbow, knee.</p>


<p>The art of eight limbs sounds cool and all but once you break out of the male brovado you can see it is very rigid non flowing with weak boxing</p>


<p>Training as a young lad in my first Karate classes we learned how to move, circle, and switch stances with grace.</p>


<p>In fact I had to learn this lesson the hard way as I was frequently backed up in a straight line in aw as to what was coming at me</p>


<p>Another lesson I learned was SPAR THE BLACK BELTS WITHOUT FEAR! But that is for another day</p>


<p>This was further compounded by my introduction to American Kickboxing</p>


